const body = "---\ntitle: Keyboard shortcuts\ndescription: The default key for every command that has one, and how to change it.\ntype: reference\n---\n\n# Keyboard shortcuts {#keyboard-shortcuts}\n\nThese are the defaults. Every one of them can be changed in **File > Settings > Bindings**, which also lists the commands that have no key until you give them one.\n\n**Ctrl** here means the platform's menu key: Control on Linux and Windows, Command on macOS.\n\n## Files {#files}\n\n| Command | Key |\n| --- | --- |\n| New Document | Ctrl+N |\n| Open a file | Ctrl+O |\n| Save current file | Ctrl+S |\n| Save all files | Ctrl+Shift+S |\n| Close current file | Ctrl+W |\n| Close all files | Ctrl+Shift+W |\n\n## Views and panels {#views-and-panels}\n\n| Command | Key |\n| --- | --- |\n| Show the Editor view | Ctrl+Alt+E |\n| Show the Author view | Ctrl+Alt+A |\n| Show the Author view beside the source | Ctrl+Alt+S |\n| Show or hide the primary sidebar | Ctrl+B |\n| Show or hide the secondary sidebar | Ctrl+Alt+B |\n| Show or hide the bottom panel | Ctrl+J |\n| Select Document | Alt+1 |\n| Preview in Tab | Ctrl+Shift+V |\n| Preview in Split | Ctrl+Alt+P |\n\n## Editing {#editing}\n\n| Command | Key |\n| --- | --- |\n| Undo last edit | Ctrl+Z |\n| Redo previous undo | Ctrl+Y |\n| Cut | Ctrl+X |\n| Copy | Ctrl+C |\n| Paste | Ctrl+V |\n| Select All | Ctrl+A |\n| Indent | Tab |\n| Unindent | Shift+Tab |\n\n## Finding and moving {#finding-and-moving}\n\n| Command | Key |\n| --- | --- |\n| Find in current document | Ctrl+F |\n| Replace in current document | Ctrl+H |\n| Goto line number | Ctrl+G |\n| Moves to beginning of data | Ctrl+Home |\n| Moves to end of data | Ctrl+End |\n| Moves to beginning of next word | Ctrl+Right |\n| Moves to beginning of previous word | Ctrl+Left |\n| Toggle bookmark | Ctrl+M |\n| Select Bookmark | Ctrl+Shift+B |\n\n## Markup {#markup}\n\n| Command | Key |\n| --- | --- |\n| Tag | Ctrl+T |\n| Repeat last Tag | Ctrl+Shift+T |\n| Rename an Element | Ctrl+R |\n| Expand an empty Element | Ctrl+L |\n| Add a comment | Ctrl+K |\n| Insert Special Character | Ctrl+I |\n| Select Element | Ctrl+E |\n| Select Element Content | Ctrl+Shift+E |\n| Select Fragment | Ctrl+Shift+Space |\n| Goto start tag | Ctrl+Up |\n| Goto end tag | Ctrl+Down |\n| Goto next Attribute value | Ctrl+Shift+Down |\n| Goto previous Attribute value | Ctrl+Shift+Up |\n\n## Changing a key {#changing-a-key}\n\nSelect **File > Settings > Bindings**, find the command (typing in the filter box narrows the list) and select **Change…**. Press the combination you want. Escape on its own cancels; Escape with a modifier is a combination like any other, so Ctrl+Escape can be bound.\n\n**Bind nothing** leaves a command with no key. **Reset** restores one command's default, **Reset all** restores every default.\n\nOnly the keys you change are saved, so a command whose default improves in a later release follows the new one unless you have chosen something yourself. If you pick a key another command already uses, the editor says which.\n";
